    "notes": [
      "VCC from a 5 V supply, VIO from the microcontroller's supply (3.3 V): TXD, RXD and S then work at the MCU's levels without level shifting.",
      "Terminate the bus at its two ends only: 120 ohm across CANH-CANL, or split into 2 x 60 ohm with 4.7 nF to GND at the midpoint."
    ],
    "page": "Fig 6, typical application of the TJA1051T/3 (p. 13)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Decouple VCC and VIO with 100 nF each next to the pins.",
    "S low (or a GPIO) for normal mode; S has an internal pull-down, so leaving it open also gives normal mode, but tie it to GND on a board.",
    "Route CANH/CANL as a pair to the connector; add a CAN-rated TVS at the connector on harsh buses."
  ],
